"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94519-i20240701-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94519-i20240701","date":"2024-07-01","original_code":"746.1205(a)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-08-15","finding":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity: Supervision was compromised when a child was able to exit the classroom door to the playground.  This resulted in the child being on the playground alone for approximately 7-8 minutes.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026546077","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94519-i20240701-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94519-i20240701","date":"2024-07-01","original_code":"746.1201(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-08-15","finding":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited: Neglectful supervision occurred when a child was able to exit the classroom door.  The child was able to get outside to the playground for approximately seven-eight minutes without being noticed by staff. Administration retrieved the child after a parent notified them that she was outside. The child was returned inside unharmed.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026546075","violation_type_title":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited (26 TAC §746.1201(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94519-i20240701-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-307-b-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94519-i202